Let $\varphi : R 	o S$ be a ring map. Let $\mathfrak p$ be a prime of $R$. The following are equivalent  egin{enumerate} \item $\mathfrak p$ is in the image of $\Spec(S) 	o \Spec(R)$, \item $S \otimes_R \kappa(\mathfrak p) 
ot = 0$, \item $S_{\mathfrak p}/\mathfrak p S_{\mathfrak p} 
ot = 0$, \item $(S/\mathfrak pS)_{\mathfrak p} 
ot = 0$, and \item $\mathfrak p = \varphi^{-1}(\mathfrak pS)$. \end{enumerate}

Let $$ \xymatrix{ Y_2 \ar[d]_{f_2} \ar[r] & Y_1 \ar[d]^{f_1} \ X_2 \ar[r] & X_1 } $$ be a commutative diagram of morphisms of schemes. Assume $f_1$, $f_2$ quasi-compact and quasi-separated. Let $f_i = 
u_i \circ f_i'$, $i = 1, 2$ be the canonical factorizations, where $
u_i : X_i' 	o X_i$ is the normalization of $X_i$ in $Y_i$. Then there exists a unique arrow $X'_2 	o X'_1$ fitting into a commutative diagram $$ \xymatrix{ Y_2 \ar[d]_{f_2'} \ar[r] & Y_1 \ar[d]^{f_1'} \ X_2' \ar[d]_{
u_2} \ar[r] & X_1' \ar[d]^{
u_1} \ X_2 \ar[r] & X_1 } $$
